>  Phase cap = ceil(1.25 × projection) for the five measured phases. There is ONE budget: the global cap = the sum of all phase caps, which must be ≤ 3600. That makes a global abort with every phase under its cap impossible. K1: the global cap of 3600 CPU-s decides. If the cumulative CPU-s exceed 3600, the run is INVALID, even if every phase is under its own cap (by construction this cannot happen as long as the sum of the caps is ≤ 3600). Gate: sum ≤ 3600, i.e. measured projections ≤ (3600 − 260) / 1.25 = 2672 CPU-s. If it does not fit, the v8.2 ladder applies (adaptation, in-distribution, tuning, in that order; λ and structure grids are never shrunk). If it still does not fit: NOT_LAUNCHED, and the numbers go to dahill and mixxy. K2: R = P_fits / 336.8 is reported. Because every phase is projected from full-size per-unit costs measured in the probe (C2c), no toy projection goes into the gate. If R > 1.5 and one of the phases tuning, test, in_distribution or adaptation is measured more than 20% below its toy projection × R, that phase's projection is set to toy projection × R (the larger value counts) before the gate. The values go into CONFIG_v8.3 only after the probe. The plan stays unchanged.
